exports[`pathological fixture two cards share a name across types 1`] = `
"ERROR CL0622 Codex/items.cl.yaml
  story cards named "Shared Name" collide on branch "main" (character in items.cl.yaml and location in items.cl.yaml). Velvet Lattice merges story cards by name, so only one survives to AID and which one is position-dependent under inheritance. Give them distinct names.
WARN CL0630 compile.cl.yaml
  branch "main" resolves no opening: and no adventureDescription:, so Velvet Lattice would start this leaf with an empty prompt. Give the branch an opening:, or one an ancestor passes down.
WARN CL0631 compile.cl.yaml
  branch "main" resolves no aiInstructions:. Velvet Lattice writes an empty-string AI Instructions on AID's side for it, and an empty string suppresses AID's model-default instructions rather than falling back to them — the leaf plays with none at all. Give the branch an aiInstructions:, or one an ancestor passes down.
WARN CL0628 Codex/items.cl.yaml
  aid.type " Gadget" has leading whitespace; writing it as "Gadget". Remove the whitespace.
  hint: A leading space survives in a directory name, so the type would reach AI Dungeon as a category whose name differs from the obvious one by an invisible character.
ERROR CL0626 Codex/items.cl.yaml
  aid.type values "Widget" and "widget" differ only by case, and are written to the same file on a case-insensitive filesystem. Rename one type.
  hint: Story Cards/{type}/{type}.md is one path for all of them on Windows and macOS, so the group written last overwrites the others and their cards never reach AI Dungeon. Pick one spelling."
`;
